t_meta\">\n\t\t\t\t\t\t<a class=\"author_inline\" data-locale-id=\"en\" href=\"\/matlabcentral\/profile\/authors\/3266642\">\n\t\t\t\t\t\t<img class=\"add_border_radius_50 remove_border community_profile_image\" src=\"\/responsive_image\/75\/75\/0\/0\/0\/profile\/3266642?s_tid=mlc_recom_user\">Majid Al-Sirafi<\/a> in <a href=\"\/matlabcentral\/answers\/index?s_tid=mlc_recom_appindex\"> MATLAB Answers<\/a> on 24 September 2012\n\t\t\t\t\t<\/span>\n\t\t\t\t\t<p class=\"post_body\"> Hi everyone how can I delete element from vector .... for example a=[1,2,3,4,5] how can I delete 3 from above vector to be a=[1,2,4,5] thank you majid kA03q0000015JgHCAU 000178401<\/p>\n\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t<\/div>\n\t\t\t\t<div class=\"col-xs-12 col-sm-3 text-center add_vertical_align_middle add_margin_10_xs mb-2\"><div class=\"community_panel panel panel-default add_margin_0 add_border_color_green add_font_color_green replies-box pull-left pull_right_lg pull_right_md pull_right_sm\"><div class=\"panel-body\"><p class=\"answers-count\">8<\/p><p class=\"answers-count-label\">answers<\/p><\/div><\/div><\/div>\n\t\t\t<\/div>\n\t\t\t<div class=\"row\"><div class=\"meta-data col-xs-12\"><ul class=\"list-unstyled list-inline add_display_inline small mb-0\"><li class=\"list-inline-item\"><span class=\"icon-like icon_16\"><\/span>   11<\/li><li class=\"list-inline-item add_indent_10\"><span class=\"icon-watch icon_16\"><\/span>   531<\/li><li class=\"list-inline-item add_indent_10\"><span class=\"icon-feedback icon_16\"><\/span> 7<\/li><\/ul><\/div><\/div>\n\t\t<\/div>\n\t<\/div>\n\t<div class=\"panel panel-default home-content-card recommendation_card\">\n\t\t<div class=\"panel-body\">\n\t\t\t<div class=\"row\">\n\t\t\t\t<div class=\"col-xs-12\">\n\t\t\t\t\t<h4 class=\"add_font_arial\">\n\t\t\t\t\t\t<strong>\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t<a class=\"card-title\" href=\"\/matlabcentral\/cody\/problems\/566-sum-of-first-n-terms-of-a-harmonic-progression?s_tid=mlc_recom_leaf\">Sum of first n terms of a harmonic progression<\/a>\n\t\t\t\t\t\t<\/strong>\n\t\t\t\t\t<\/h4>\n\t\t\t\t<\/div>\n\t\t\t<\/div>\n\t\t\t<div class=\"row\">\n\t\t\t\t<div class=\"col-xs-12 col-sm-9 remove_margin_5 add_text_wrapping\">\n\t\t\t\t\t<span class=\"post_meta\">\n\t\t\t\t\t\t<a class=\"author_inline\" data-locale-id=\"en\" href=\"\/matlabcentral\/profile\/authors\/3162046\">\n\t\t\t\t\t\t<img class=\"add_border_radius_50 remove_border community_profile_image\" src=\"\/responsive_image\/75\/75\/0\/0\/0\/profile\/3162046?s_tid=mlc_recom_user\">Srivardhini<\/a> in <a href=\"\/matlabcentral\/cody?s_tid=mlc_recom_appindex\"> Cody<\/a> on 08 April 2012\n\t\t\t\t\t<\/span>\n\t\t\t\t\t<p class=\"post_body\">Sum of first n terms of a harmonic progression Given inputs a, d and n, return the sum of the first n terms of the harmonic progression a, a\/(1+d), a\/(1+2d), a\/(1+3d),.... %%a=1;d=1;n=1;y_correct = 1;assert(isequal(harmonicSum(a,d,n),y_correct));%%a=2;d=2;n=5;y_correct = round(3.5746,4);assert(isequ...<\/p>\n\t\t\t\t\t<div class=\"tag_list remove_margin_10 add_margin_10\"><span class=\"tag-label\">Tags: <\/span><ul class=\"list-unstyled list-inline add_display_inline\"><li><a href=\"\/matlabcentral\/cody\/problems?term=tag:'series'&s_tid=mlc_lp_tag\" rel=\"nofollow\">series<\/a><\/li><li><a href=\"\/matlabcentral\/cody\/problems?term=tag:'sequences'&s_tid=mlc_lp_tag\" rel=\"nofollow\">sequences<\/a><\/li><li><a href=\"\/matlabcentral\/cody\/problems?term=tag:'series'&s_tid=mlc_lp_tag\" rel=\"nofollow\">series<\/a><\/li><\/ul><\/div>\n\t\t\t\t<\/div>\n\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t<\/div>\n\t\t\t<div class=\"row\"><div class=\"meta-data col-xs-12\"><ul class=\"list-unstyled list-inline add_display_inline small mb-0\"><li class=\"list-inline-item\"><span class=\"icon-account icon_16\"><\/span>   520<\/li><li class=\"list-inline-item add_indent_10\"><span class=\"icon-like icon_16\"><\/span>   3<\/li><li class=\"list-inline-item add_indent_10\"><span class=\"icon-feedback icon_16\"><\/span> 14<\/li><\/ul><\/div><\/div>\n\t\t<\/div>\n\t<\/div>\n\t<div class=\"panel panel-default home-content-card recommendation_card\">\n\t\t<div class=\"panel-body\">\n\t\t\t<div class=\"row\">\n\t\t\t\t<div class=\"col-xs-12\">\n\t\t\t\t\t<h4 class=\"add_font_arial\">\n\t\t\t\t\t\t<strong>\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t<a class=\"card-title\" href=\"\/matlabcentral\/answers\/23162-contious-time-model-linear-analysis-toolbox?s_tid=mlc_recom_leaf\">contious time model - linear analysis toolbox<\/a>\n\t\t\t\t\t\t<\/strong>\n\t\t\t\t\t<\/h4>\n\t\t\t\t<\/div>\n\t\t\t<\/div>\n\t\t\t<div class=\"row\">\n\t\t\t\t<div class=\"col-xs-12 col-sm-9 remove_margin_5 add_text_wrapping\">\n\t\t\t\t\t<span class=\"post_meta\">\n\t\t\t\t\t\t<a class=\"author_inline\" data-locale-id=\"en\" href=\"\/matlabcentral\/profile\/authors\/2247917\">\n\t\t\t\t\t\t<img class=\"add_border_radius_50 remove_border community_profile_image\" src=\"\/responsive_image\/75\/75\/0\/0\/0\/profile\/2247917?s_tid=mlc_recom_user\">Jamie<\/a> in <a href=\"\/matlabcentral\/answers\/index?s_tid=mlc_recom_appindex\"> MATLAB Answers<\/a> on 06 December 2011\n\t\t\t\t\t<\/span>\n\t\t\t\t\t<p class=\"post_body\">I&#39;ve been using the linear analysis toolbox quite a bit lately for generating linear models within simulink. &gt;&gt; Tools \/ control design \/ linear analysis.. For some reason the models generated are generally discrete. I appreciate that their are a few functions for shifting between discrete...<\/p>\n\t\t\t\t\t<div class=\"tag_list remove_margin_10 add_margin_10\"><span class=\"tag-label\">Tags: <\/span><ul class=\"list-unstyled list-inline add_display_inline\"><li><a href=\"\/matlabcentral\/answers\/?term=tag:'generating continous time models from the &#39;linear analysis&#39; gui'&s_tid=mlc_lp_tag\" rel=\"nofollow\">generating continous time models from the &#39;linear analysis&#39; gui<\/a><\/li><\/ul><\/div>\n\t\t\t\t<\/div>\n\t\t\t\t<div class=\"col-xs-12 col-sm-3 text-center add_vertical_align_middle add_margin_10_xs mb-2\"><div class=\"community_panel panel panel-default add_margin_0 add_border_color_green add_font_color_green replies-box pull-left pull_right_lg pull_right_md pull_right_sm\"><div class=\"panel-body\"><p class=\"answers-count\">1<\/p><p class=\"answers-count-label\">answer<\/p><\/div><\/div><\/div>\n\t\t\t<\/div>\n\t\t\t<div class=\"row\"><div class=\"meta-data col-xs-12\"><ul class=\"list-unstyled list-inline add_display_inline small mb-0\"><li class=\"list-inline-item\"><span class=\"icon-like icon_16\"><\/span>   0<\/li><li class=\"list-inline-item add_indent_10\"><span class=\"icon-watch icon_16\"><\/span>   389<\/li><li class=\"list-inline-item add_indent_10\"><span class=\"icon-feedback icon_16\"><\/span> 0<\/li><\/ul><\/div><\/div>\n\t\t<\/div>\n\t<\/div>\n\t<div class=\"panel panel-default home-content-card recommendation_card\">\n\t\t<div class=\"panel-body\">\n\t\t\t<div class=\"row\">\n\t\t\t\t<div class=\"col-xs-12\">\n\t\t\t\t\t<h4 class=\"add_font_arial\">\n\t\t\t\t\t\t<strong>\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t<a class=\"card-title\" href=\"https:\/\/blogs.mathworks.com\/cleve\/2019\/06\/24\/bohemian-matrices-in-the-matlab-gallery\/?s_tid=mlc_recom_leaf\">Bohemian Matrices in the MATLAB\u00AE Gallery<\/a>\n\t\t\t\t\t\t<\/strong>\n\t\t\t\t\t<\/h4>\n\t\t\t\t<\/div>\n\t\t\t<\/div>\n\t\t\t<div class=\"row\">\n\t\t\t\t<div class=\"col-xs-12 col-sm-9 remove_margin_5 add_text_wrapping\">\n\t\t\t\t\t<span class=\"post_meta\">\n\t\t\t\t\t\t<a class=\"author_inline\" data-locale-id=\"en\" href=\"https:\/\/www.mathworks.com\/matlabcentral\/profile\/authors\/349729\">\n\t\t\t\t\t\t<img class=\"add_border_radius_50 remove_border community_profile_image\" src=\"\/responsive_image\/75\/75\/0\/0\/0\/profile\/349729?s_tid=mlc_recom_user\">Cleve Moler<\/a> in <a href=\"https:\/\/blogs.mathworks.com\/cleve?s_tid=mlc_recom_appindex\"> Blogs<\/a> on 24 June 2019\n\t\t\t\t\t<\/span>\n\t\t\t\t\t<p class=\"post_body\">We will have a two-part minisymposium on &quot;Bohemian Matrices&quot; at ICIAM2019, the International Congress on Industrial and Applied Mathematics in Valencia, Spain, July 15-19. This is an outline of my talk.<\/p>\n\t\t\t\t\t<div class=\"tag_list remove_margin_10 add_margin_10\"><span class=\"tag-label\">Categories: <\/span><ul class=\"list-unstyled list-inline add_display_inline\"><li><a href=\"https:\/\/blogs.mathworks.com\/cleve\/category\/eigenvalues\/?&s_tid=mlc_lp_tag\" rel=\"nofollow\">Eigenvalues<\/a><\/li><li><a href=\"https:\/\/blogs.mathworks.com\/cleve\/category\/history\/?&s_tid=mlc_lp_tag\" rel=\"nofollow\">History<\/a><\/li><li><a href=\"https:\/\/blogs.mathworks.com\/cleve\/category\/matrices\/?&s_tid=mlc_lp_tag\" rel=\"nofollow\">Matrices<\/a><\/li><li><a href=\"https:\/\/blogs.mathworks.com\/cleve\/category\/numerical-analysis\/?&s_tid=mlc_lp_tag\" rel=\"nofollow\">Numerical Analysis<\/a><\/li><li><a href=\"https:\/\/blogs.mathworks.com\/cleve\/category\/people\/?&s_tid=mlc_lp_tag\" rel=\"nofollow\">People<\/a><\/li><\/ul><\/div>\n\t\t\t\t<\/div>\n\t\t\t\t<div class=\"col-xs-12 col-sm-3 text-center add_vertical_align_middle img_wrapper add_margin_10_xs\"><img class=\"preview_img pull-left pull_right_lg pull_right_md pull_right_sm\" src=\"https:\/\/blogs.mathworks.com\/cleve\/wp-content\/blogs.dir\/9\/files\/bohemian_blog_01.png\" alt=\"Thumbnail\"><\/div>\n\t\t\t<\/div>\n\t\t\t<div class=\"row\"><div class=\"meta-data col-xs-12\"><ul class=\"list-unstyled list-inline add_display_inline small mb-0\"><li class=\"list-inline-item add_indent_10\"><span class=\"icon-watch icon_16\"><\/span>   145<\/li><li class=\"list-inline-item add_indent_10\"><span class=\"icon-feedback icon_16\"><\/span> 0<\/li><\/ul><\/div><\/div>\n\t\t<\/div>\n\t<\/div>\n\t<div class=\"panel panel-default home-content-card recommendation_card\">\n\t\t<div class=\"panel-body\">\n\t\t\t<div class=\"row\">\n\t\t\t\t<div class=\"col-xs-12\">\n\t\t\t\t\t<h4 class=\"add_font_arial\">\n\t\t\t\t\t\t<strong>\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t<a class=\"card-title\" href=\"https:\/\/blogs.mathw